<body lang=3DEN-GB style=3D'tab-interval:36.0pt;word-wrap:break-word'>

<div class=3DWordSection1>

<p class=3DMsoNormal>We have Income which is made up from the annual figure=
 for<o:p></o:p></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal>Assets<o:p></o:p></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal>Income<o:p></o:p></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal>Cash<o:p></o:p></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal>Savings<o:p></o:p></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal>Bonds<o:p></o:p></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal>Stocks and Shares<o:p></o:p></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal>The outgoings are <o:p></o:p></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal>Annual Salary which we pay ourselves from our savings =
for
discretionary spending<o:p></o:p></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal>Annual Expenses<o:p></o:p></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal>The inflation figure is in txtbx_inflation and is how =
much
the Annual Expenses will increase by each year<o:p></o:p></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal>At this stage I have added a column chart called
chart_overall to the panel called panel_overall_graph. I think this should =
be a
column chart but please do tell me if there is a better one to use. This gr=
aph
should show the value that will be available each of the years based on the
number of years that has been written in the txtbx_length. Each column will=
 be
for one year. We can see the persons age in txtbx_age so we may want to
annotate the x-axis with the age. As an example if the users says they are =
60years
old and txtbx_length is set to 40 then we would have 40 columns starting at=
 60
years old all the way to 100 years old.<o:p></o:p></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal>Here is an example on how to calculate the value of ea=
ch
column starting with year 1. Do you think we need to add a table or file to
store this data in as we work out each year?:<o:p></o:p></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal>Available funds:<o:p></o:p></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal>Assets =3D =A3100,000.00<o:p></o:p></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal>Income =3D =A310,000.00<o:p></o:p></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal>Cash =3D =A38,000.00<o:p></o:p></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal>Savings =3D =A360,000.00<o:p></o:p></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal>Bonds =3D =A3150,000.00<o:p></o:p></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal>Stocks and Shares =3D =A36576.00<o:p></o:p></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal>Outgoings:<o:p></o:p></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal>Annual salary =3D =A320,000.00<o:p></o:p></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal>Annual Expenses =3D =A38,214.00<o:p></o:p></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal>We will need to go to the &quot;future expenses&quot; =
and
&quot;future income&quot; and look at which items are relevant for the year=
 we
are going to draw in the chart as we will need to add or subtract them befo=
re
we draw the column for the year we are drawing<o:p></o:p></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal>This means that we have available funds of =A3334,576.=
00 with
expenses of =A328,214.00. The column in the chart for year one will be
=A3334,576.00 - =A328,214.00 =3D =A3306,362.00. we draw =A3306,362.00.<o:p>=
</o:p></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal>For year 2 our available funds will be =A3306,362.00 +=
 any
relevant items in future income dataGridView which we say are =A312,000.00 =
but
our expenses will be =A328,214.00 which need to be increased by inflation. =
If
inflation was 10% then expenses will now be =A328,214.00 + =A32,821.40 =3D
=A331,035.40. The column we now draw will be =A3306,362.00 + =A312,000.00 -
=A331,035.40 =3D =A3287,326.60 and this we draw into the column.<o:p></o:p>=
</p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal>What we did in Year 2 we now do in Year 3, 4 up to the=
 last
year that the user choose in txtbx_length. The column can go negative.<o:p>=
</o:p></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal>When we click on the button btn_draw_overall_chart the=
 chart
is drawn. We must redraw the chart when any of the following are changed. Do
you think we can redraw the chart in realtime or do we need some sot of del=
ay?
If we have not yet drawn the chart but change any of these then nothing sho=
uld
happen.<o:p></o:p></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal>thinsldr_salary<o:p></o:p></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal>txtbx_salary<o:p></o:p></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal>thinsldr_Age<o:p></o:p></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal>txtbx_age<o:p></o:p></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal>thinsldr_Length<o:p></o:p></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal>txtbx_length<o:p></o:p></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal>txtbx_inflation<o:p></o:p></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal>If any of the data in Assets or Expenses is changed th=
en we
need to click the btn_draw_overall_chart to redraw the chart. Here is some =
of
the cod to show what we have done so far. Let me know if you need any other
files please.</p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal>Thanks for your help I would now like to add a few
enhancements some of which you suggest: </p>

