stored by <b>age</b> instead of calendar year, then you=92d flip it and use
currentAge in SumRows. But with 4&#8209;digit years in the grid,
DateTime.Now.Year + i is the right approach.<o:p></o:p></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal>Yesterday<o:p></o:p></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal>Nice job it is working well now thanks. Now I need som=
e help
to add the next bit, I am not sure what is the best way to do this so let me
explain my thoughts to you. In UK a person will get a state pension. The age
you get this at and the amount you get varies so I think I will let the user
add this to the future earnings Datagridview manually. The amount you get
increases every year by what is called the triple lock. The triple lock is =
the
government=92s commitment that the State Pension will rise every April by
whichever is highest: <span style=3D'font-family:"Segoe UI Symbol",sans-ser=
if;
mso-bidi-font-family:"Segoe UI Symbol"'>&#10004;</span> CPI inflation measu=
red
in the previous September <span style=3D'font-family:"Segoe UI Symbol",sans=
-serif;
mso-bidi-font-family:"Segoe UI Symbol"'>&#10004;</span> average earnings gr=
owth
measured over May to July <span style=3D'font-family:"Segoe UI Symbol",sans=
-serif;
mso-bidi-font-family:"Segoe UI Symbol"'>&#10004;</span> or 2.5% I think tha=
t we
should look at using 2.5% as this is a known figure and possibly the lowest
that this can ever be. I expect the user to manually add this once into the
future earnings DataGridView but somehow to tell the software that it is the
state pension, maybe a tick box? We can then use this figure and increase i=
t by
2.5% for every year after. Do you think it is possible to add this value
increasing it in the April of each year which means 3 months at the previous
rate then 9 months at that rate plus 2.5%. This seems complicated to me but=
 I
am sure you will be able to show me an easy way to do it.<o:p></o:p></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal>Stephen, this is a <i>really</i> good next step =97 an=
d you=92re
thinking about it exactly the way a financial modeller would. The UK State
Pension =93triple lock=94 is awkward because it increases <b>part&#8209;yea=
r at the
old rate</b> and <b>part&#8209;year at the new rate</b>, and you want to
integrate this into your future income grid in a way that is:<o:p></o:p></p>

<ul style=3D'margin-top:0cm' type=3Ddisc>
 <li class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'mso-list:l37 level1 lfo89;tab-stops:list 36=
.0pt'>simple
     for the user<o:p></o:p></li>
 <li class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'mso-list:l37 level1 lfo89;tab-stops:list 36=
.0pt'>simple
     for you to code<o:p></o:p></li>
 <li class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'mso-list:l37 level1 lfo89;tab-stops:list 36=
.0pt'>accurate
     enough for retirement modelling<o:p></o:p></li>
 <li class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'mso-list:l37 level1 lfo89;tab-stops:list 36=
.0pt'>flexible
     for future enhancements<o:p></o:p></li>
</ul>

<p class=3DMsoNormal>Let me show you the cleanest, most robust way to do th=
is.<o:p></o:p></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><b><span style=3D'font-family:"Segoe UI Emoji",sans-se=
rif;
mso-bidi-font-family:"Segoe UI Emoji"'>&#11088;</span> The key idea:<o:p></=
o:p></b></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><b>Let the user enter ONE row for State Pension, tick =
a box,
and your code automatically expands it into future years.<o:p></o:p></b></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal>This avoids:<o:p></o:p></p>

<ul style=3D'margin-top:0cm' type=3Ddisc>
 <li class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'mso-list:l74 level1 lfo90;tab-stops:list 36=
.0pt'>the
     user manually entering 30=9640 rows<o:p></o:p></li>
 <li class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'mso-list:l74 level1 lfo90;tab-stops:list 36=
.0pt'>mistakes
     in inflation/triple&#8209;lock calculations<o:p></o:p></li>
 <li class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'mso-list:l74 level1 lfo90;tab-stops:list 36=
.0pt'>clutter
     in the future income grid<o:p></o:p></li>
 <li class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'mso-list:l74 level1 lfo90;tab-stops:list 36=
.0pt'>confusion
     about calendar years vs ages<o:p></o:p></li>
</ul>

<p class=3DMsoNormal>You keep the UI simple, and your code does the heavy
lifting.<o:p></o:p></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><b><span style=3D'font-family:"Segoe UI Emoji",sans-se=
rif;
mso-bidi-font-family:"Segoe UI Emoji"'>&#11088;</span> Step 1 =97 Add a che=
ckbox
to mark the row as =93State Pension=94<o:p></o:p></b></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal>Add a checkbox column to dgv_future_income:<o:p></o:p>=
</p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal>csharp<o:p></o:p></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal>var chk =3D new DataGridViewCheckBoxColumn();<o:p></o:=
p></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal>chk.Name =3D &quot;IsStatePension&quot;;<o:p></o:p></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal>chk.HeaderText =3D &quot;State Pension?&quot;;<o:p></o=
:p></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal>dgv_future_income.Columns.Add(chk);<o:p></o:p></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal>Now each future income row has:<o:p></o:p></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal>| Description | Year | Amount | State Pension? |<o:p><=
/o:p></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal>The user will:<o:p></o:p></p>

<ul style=3D'margin-top:0cm' type=3Ddisc>
 <li class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'mso-list:l68 level1 lfo91;tab-stops:list 36=
.0pt'>add
     <b>one</b> row<o:p></o:p></li>
 <li class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'mso-list:l68 level1 lfo91;tab-stops:list 36=
.0pt'>set
     Year =3D the year they reach State Pension age<o:p></o:p></li>
 <li class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'mso-list:l68 level1 lfo91;tab-stops:list 36=
.0pt'>set
     Amount =3D first year=92s pension<o:p></o:p></li>
 <li class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'mso-list:l68 level1 lfo91;tab-stops:list 36=
.0pt'>tick
     =93State Pension?=94<o:p></o:p></li>
</ul>

<p class=3DMsoNormal>That=92s it.<o:p></o:p></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><b><span style=3D'font-family:"Segoe UI Emoji",sans-se=
rif;
mso-bidi-font-family:"Segoe UI Emoji"'>&#11088;</span> Step 2 =97 Triple lo=
ck
logic (2.5% minimum)<o:p></o:p></b></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal>Triple lock is:<o:p></o:p></p>

<ul style=3D'margin-top:0cm' type=3Ddisc>
 <li class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'mso-list:l79 level1 lfo92;tab-stops:list 36=
.0pt'>CPI
     inflation (unknown)<o:p></o:p></li>
 <li class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'mso-list:l79 level1 lfo92;tab-stops:list 36=
.0pt'>earnings
     growth (unknown)<o:p></o:p></li>
 <li class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'mso-list:l79 level1 lfo92;tab-stops:list 36=
.0pt'><b>2.5%
     minimum</b><o:p></o:p></li>
</ul>

<p class=3DMsoNormal>Since you don=92t know CPI or earnings growth, using <=
b>2.5%
every year</b> is the correct modelling choice.<o:p></o:p></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal>But you also asked:<o:p></o:p></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal>=93Can we increase it in April each year, meaning 3 mo=
nths at
old rate and 9 months at new rate?=94<o:p></o:p></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal>Yes =97 and it=92s easy.<o:p></o:p></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><b><span style=3D'font-family:"Segoe UI Symbol",sans-s=
erif;
mso-bidi-font-family:"Segoe UI Symbol"'>&#10004;</span> Formula for April
uplift:<o:p></o:p></b></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal>Let:<o:p></o:p></p>

<ul style=3D'margin-top:0cm' type=3Ddisc>
 <li class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'mso-list:l69 level1 lfo93;tab-stops:list 36=
.0pt'>P
     =3D pension amount last year<o:p></o:p></li>
 <li class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'mso-list:l69 level1 lfo93;tab-stops:list 36=
.0pt'>r
     =3D triple lock rate (0.025)<o:p></o:p></li>
</ul>

<p class=3DMsoNormal>Then:<o:p></o:p></p>

<ul style=3D'margin-top:0cm' type=3Ddisc>
 <li class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'mso-list:l83 level1 lfo94;tab-stops:list 36=
.0pt'>Jan=96Mar:
     3 months at P<o:p></o:p></li>
 <li class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'mso-list:l83 level1 lfo94;tab-stops:list 36=
.0pt'>Apr=96Dec:
     9 months at P * (1 + r)<o:p></o:p></li>
</ul>

